i7Owr13_k8So2SfkAFf3seTgP-v2cdJgA&oe=69A41D4B"}, {"file_name": "migrated_image.png", "id": "2362415107383295", "uri": "https://scontent-ord5-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/12448837_1712346882351320_445814653_n.png?_nc_cat=108&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=XgxmqggApxAQ7kNvwGfCdgZ&_nc_oc=AdmyNGqA_oFx3vYDiO3jBaqwIdq5B8FbEwzPLBhjN50OwtgtsKk4gsYneLmp9hXKeNU&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-1.oculuscdn.com&oh=00_Afucerwf4Hl37DRISsBcVrvTF-rdGzTLUZnONf0ZK7QHug&oe=69A44261"}, {"file_name": "migrated_image.png", "id": "668669003899669", "uri": "https://scontent-ord5-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/12448842_1552150631781687_1259563216_n.png?_nc_cat=108&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=QWeWltru8PUQ7kNvwHBYSso&_nc_oc=AdmMcS0mB9TsdG1CLgO1_MxEQ7UU_L67ynYlmFzzxVXPMIyl8LqqhkIjFhBXvZ4--kg&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-1.oculuscdn.com&oh=00_AfvIStkCG-Zu0ihT5EYRVtLpmghDpNi9gSleVGtsSmfGwQ&oe=69A4526F"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": null, "display_name": "Window to the World", "keywords": ["photography", "art", "landscape", "transmedia", "experimental"], "long_description": "As a photographer and VR enthusiast I have always dreamed about a way of expressing photography as close as possible to the actual moment of capture, about the moment when reality and photography converge. The first trial was a couple of years ago when I took some photos and made a short film based on the famous parallax techniques but with a twist. The twist was that everything was now in actual 3d and not just 2D layers. The next step was giving the viewer a bit of input and so came to be the online WebGL version. The final step was full immersion; VR was only the natural step forward. \nmore info on how this was achieved : http://aurelm.com/2013/12/15/fernweh-3d-parallax-photography-tutorial/", "short_description": "This is a photographic experiment. It represents what can be achieved using classical landscape photography and virtual reality as means of expression. "}]}, "developer_name": null, "dev